In plain terms
--------------
You are free to:

* Share  — copy and redistribute these documents, in any medium or format.
* Adapt  — remix, transform, build on them (your own palette tables, your own
  skill files, your own house style derived from these rules).

Under the following terms:

* Attribution — you must give appropriate credit and indicate if changes were
  made. A sufficient credit line:

      Quiet Nature Poster (lite) by feralcrow, CC BY-NC 4.0
      https://github.com/feralcrow/quiet-nature-poster

  Keep the credit where people will actually see it: in the file that carries
  the rules, or in your skill's README, not buried in a commit message.
* NonCommercial — you may not use these documents for commercial purposes.
  Selling the rule library, packaging it inside a paid product, or gating it
  behind a subscription is not allowed. Using the system to do paid design work
  for a client is fine — see "What this licence does not cover" below.
* No additional restrictions — you may not apply legal terms or technological
  measures that restrict what others may do with the shared documents.

What this licence does not cover
--------------------------------
* The outputs. Posters, images, prompts, titles and palette proposals you
  generate with this system are yours. You may sell them, print them, ship them
  in client work and license them as you like. Credit is appreciated, not
  required.
* Any third-party material referenced here (font names, film-stock or paper
  references, AI model behaviour). Fonts carry their own licences — check them
  before shipping anything commercially.
* The photographic or artwork references that inspired the rules. They are not
  included in this repository and are not licensed by this document.

If you want a commercial licence for the rule library itself (to resell it,
bundle it in a paid product, or use it as training data), open an issue on the
repository or contact the author.
